                  %a{:href => "#grothendieck_connection"} Grothendieck connection
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#dmodules"} D-modules
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#infinitesimal_path_groupoids"}
                    Infinitesimal path
                    = succeed "-groupoids" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In a context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-geometry"} D-geometry
            %em de Rham space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dR
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dR(X)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that identifies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimally close points
          %p
            It is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreduced+object"} coreduced reflection
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#on_
            On
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Rings
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rings^{op}
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in CRing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in R
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilradical"} nilradical
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            consisting of the nilpotent elements. The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to R/I
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by the ideal corresponds in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}
            to the inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spec (R/I) \to Spec R
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+object"} reduced
            part of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(Ring^{op})
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}
              (for instance a
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %strong de Rham space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
              is the presheaf defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                    %mo :
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi Spec
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi I
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_{dR} : Spec R \mapsto X\left(Spec \left(R/I\right)\right)
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_quotient As a quotient
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(Ring^{op})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth scheme
              then the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \to X_{dR}
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              (hence an epimorphism over each
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the relation “being infinitesimally close” between points of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi inf
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mi X
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_{dR} = \lim_\to
                    \\left(
                    X^{inf} \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} X
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              of the two projections out of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood+of+the+diagonal"} formal neighbourhood of the diagonal
          %h3#relation_to_jet_bundles Relation to jet bundles
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            along the projection map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi inf
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \longrightarrow \Pi_{inf} X
            yields its
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In terms of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+homotopy+type+theory"} differential homotopy type theory
              this means that forming “jet types” of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              operation along the unit of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi jet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mi inf
                        %mi X
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    jet(E) \coloneqq \underset{X \to \Pi_{inf}X}{\prod} E
                    \\,.
          %h3#relation_to_formally_tale_morphisms_of_schemes Relation to formally étale morphisms of schemes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} formally étale morphism of schemes
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %h3#crystalline_site Crystalline site
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : Ring \to Set
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+site"} big site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}/X_{dR}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi dR
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystalline+site"} crystalline site
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#grothendieck_connection Grothendieck connection
          %p
            Morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR} \to Mod
            encode flat higher
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
          %p
            Accordingly,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            for de Rham spaces – sometimes called
            %strong de Rham descent
            encodes flat 1-connections. This is described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+connection"} Grothendieck connection
          %h3#dmodules D-modules
          %p
            The category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-module"} D-module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            is equivalent to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on the corresponding de Rham space (
            %a{:href => "#LurieCrystal"}> Lurie, above theorem 0.4
            ).
          %h3#infinitesimal_path_groupoids
            Infinitesimal path
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+path+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} infinitesimal path ∞-groupoid
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The term
            %em de Rham space
            or
            %em de Rham stack
            apparently goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Simpson96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy over the complex numbers and generalized de Rham cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em Moduli of Vector Bundles (Taniguchi symposium December 1994)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.tib.eu/en/search/id/BLCP%3ACN013382849/Homotopy-Over-the-Complex-Numbers-and-Generalized/"} web
          %p
            But actually there it just has the notation “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi dR
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{dR}
            ” and then the functor it co-represents is called the “de Rham shape” of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p A review of the constructions is on the first two pages of
          %ul
            %li#LurieCrystal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                Notes on crystals and algebraic
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lurie-NotesOnCrystals.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The de Rham space construction on spaces (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"}> schemes
            ) is described in
            %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~teleman/math/simpson.pdf#page=7"} section 3, p. 7
          %ul
            %li#SimpsonTeleman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  de Rham theorem for
                  = succeed "-stacks" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~teleman/math/simpson.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SimpsonTelemanDeRhamTheoremForStacks.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            which goes on to assert the existence of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho Sh_\infty(C)
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
          %p
            Similar discussion in a context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Gaitsgory"}> Dennis Gaitsgory
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Rozenblyum"} Nick Rozenblyum
              %em Crystals and D-modules
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~gaitsgde/GL/Crystalstext.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The characterization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+scheme"} formally smooth scheme
            as above is also on that page.
          %p
            See also online comments by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"} David Ben-Zvi
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/04/journal_club_geometric_infinit.html#c023287"} here
            and
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/08/question_on_synthetic_differen.html#c026218"} here
            on the
            = succeed "Caf\u00E9." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/10556/d-modules-derham-spaces-and-microlocalization"} here
            on MO.
